# Doxa pipeline agent

Read [doxa-agents/AGENTS.md](doxa-agents/AGENTS.md) when changing ingestion, processing, canonicalization, or clustering code.

## After code changes

1. Edit `doxa-agents/departments/**/handler.ts` (real logic). Update `schedule.sql` only if cron schedule or job changes.
2. Update `supabase/functions/<deploy_name>/index.ts` stub only when adding a new function or changing handler path.
3. **Librarian sync** — the `stop` hook runs `npm run agents:refresh` on turn end; fix validation errors if the hook follow-up reports failure. You can also run it manually when testing mid-turn.
4. **Never hand-edit** `doxa-agents/manifest.yaml` or `doxa-agents/docs/generated/*`.
5. **Before finishing** handler/stub/worker edits: run the Bugbot review-and-fix loop in [doxa-pipeline-review.mdc](doxa-pipeline-review.mdc).

## Chunking, merging, canonicalization vs topology

- **02-chunking-engine** — chunk bodies, extract entities, chunk QA (`extract-story-entities`, `standardize-chunk-extraction`, etc.).
- **03-merging-engine** — merge to `story_*`, merge QA (`merge-story-entities`, `validate-merged-extraction`, etc.).
- **01-canonical-knowledge** (`link-canonical-*`, `update-stances`): dedupe story entities to global canonical rows.
- **02-debate-topology** onward: candidate queues, relationship classification, agreement/controversy clusters—not text extraction. See [doxa-agents/docs/topology-pipeline.md](doxa-agents/docs/topology-pipeline.md).

## Step folder naming

Pipeline steps live under `departments/<department>/<NN>-<step-id>/` (flat agent) or `departments/<department>/<workflow>/<NN>-<step-id>/` (multi-step workflow). Two-digit prefixes (`01-`, `02-`, …) sort folders in run order; `npm run agents:sync` strips the prefix for catalog step ids and `activation.yaml` entries.

## Directory layout and READMEs

Follow [doxa-agents/docs/directory-layout.md](doxa-agents/docs/directory-layout.md). Every **department**, **flat agent**, and **workflow** folder needs a `README.md` (passes `agents:validate`). Nested step folders are documented in the workflow README. Catalog sync lives in [doxa-agents/librarian](doxa-agents/librarian/) — not under `departments/`.

## Engine data purge

When adding or removing pipeline output tables, edit `doxa-agents/ops/purge-engine-tables.yaml` and run `npm run agents:refresh` (regenerates `supabase/routines/purge_engine_data.sql`). Then re-apply that routine on the deployed DB yourself (see Agent-owned ops). New installs get migration `121_purge_engine_data.sql`.

## Agent-owned ops (do these yourself — do not hand back to the user)

When credentials / CLI / MCP are available (project `.env.local`, linked `supabase` ref, Supabase MCP), **execute** the following after relevant code changes. Prefer action over reminders.

- **Migrations** — apply new `supabase/migrations/*.sql` via Supabase MCP `apply_migration` or CLI; do not ask the user to paste SQL into the dashboard.
- **Edge function deploy** — deploy touched functions yourself (CLI preferred for multi-file handlers). Use [doxa-agents/docs/generated/deploy.md](doxa-agents/docs/generated/deploy.md) for the full list.
- **Pipeline re-runs** — after deploy, invoke the changed step (or its orchestrator) with service-role auth when the change needs a data refresh to take effect.
- **Purge routine** — after `purge-engine-tables.yaml` changes and `agents:refresh`, re-apply `supabase/routines/purge_engine_data.sql` on the deployed DB (new installs still get migration `121_purge_engine_data.sql`).

**Default deploy:** `supabase functions deploy <deploy_name>`

**JWT disabled (must pass flag on every CLI deploy):** These functions use a shared secret or service-role caller instead of a user JWT. Deploying without `--no-verify-jwt` causes **401 Invalid JWT** for the Cloudflare worker callback or internal invokes.

