```bash
supabase functions deploy <deploy_name> --no-verify-jwt
```

When deploying any JWT-off function above, always include `--no-verify-jwt`. Mirror new JWT-off functions in `supabase/config.toml` as `[functions.<deploy_name>]` with `verify_jwt = false`.

## Still user-owned (cannot fully automate)

- **Secret values** in Supabase / Cloudflare dashboards (names are in [doxa-agents/docs/generated/secrets.md](doxa-agents/docs/generated/secrets.md)) — agent may name them; user must set values if missing.
- **`doxa-agents/activation.yaml`** — add step id only when the user asks to mark a workflow active (does not schedule crons).
- **pg_cron enablement** — run `schedule.sql` yourself when Vault/`project_url`/`service_role_key` are available; otherwise note the blocker briefly.

### Isolated pipeline testing

When the user is walking one article through the pipeline, use [doxa-agents/docs/pipeline-test-params.md](doxa-agents/docs/pipeline-test-params.md) for isolation POST fields (`story_id`, `story_claim_id`, etc.). Shared helpers live in `doxa-agents/lib/pipeline-test-params.ts`.

Do not update `activation.yaml` unless the user asks to enable a workflow.
